<title>BELGIUM: Farm Council to discuss durum wheat aid changes.</title>
<headline>Farm Council to discuss durum wheat aid changes.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Farm Council will discuss on Monday at Italy's request a proposal to change an aid scheme for durum wheat producers, EU officials said.</p>
<p>The Commission proposed in July fixing a maximum guaranteed area for each member state that would be shared between traditional producers.</p>
<p>It also proposed the compulsory use of certified seed and anti-fraud measures to ensure that output remained in line with the planted area.</p>
<p>In September ministers from traditional producer countries, notably Italy, demanded bigger areas while others, such as Germany and Austria, sought to be included in the scheme.</p>
<p>Officials said a decision was only possible in December after the European Parliament has given an opinion.</p>
</text>
